  "negative_results": [
    {
      "stage": "Initial execution regression",
      "cases": 64,
      "failures": 64,
      "reason": "A blanket trigger guard rejected all writes, including unrelated target tables and events."
    },
    {
      "stage": "First row-trigger executor",
      "cases": 64,
      "failures": 29,
      "reason": "Rollback full commits omitted trigger metadata after its catalog was acknowledged. INSERT preparation rejected compiler-bound OLD/NEW values inside nested expressions, and duplicate integer rowids used a generic diagnostic."
    },
    {
      "stage": "Metadata retention, bound-value preparation and actual key diagnostic",
      "cases": 132,
      "failures": 2,
      "reason": "total_changes() was incorrectly fixed for all outer rows. SQLite exposes earlier trigger-body totals to later rows; changes() retains the entry value."
    },
    {
      "stage": "Dynamic total counter and restored trigger frames",
      "cases": 132,
      "failures": 0
    },
    {
      "stage": "Lean proof and fixture compilation",
      "reason": "Captured component failures cover a reserved identifier, typed dummy values, mutable-variable shadowing, Except.map simplification and a nonreducible String.toLower constant. The final generic counter theorem states its actual name inequality precondition. Existing assertions and Core source-free semantics were retained."
    }
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "Programs are chosen by actual owner/event and the syntactic UPDATE OF assignment list. UPDATE/DELETE collect actual rowids before mutation, sort signed keys, and skip keys removed by earlier programs without re-evaluating the original WHERE. Default recursive triggers are disabled per active program name, with a structural depth bound.",
    "The existing RETURNING evaluator captures the accepted row after affinity/constraint preparation and before AFTER programs. Original user outputs are retained before body mutations. Actual lexical frames bind OLD/NEW with column affinity/collation and stored native-text provenance; SELECT uses the ordinary scalar-query source compiler.",
    "Trigger-frame changes()/last_insert_rowid() are restored after the body. Body writes contribute to total_changes immediately while direct outer writes are accounted at statement completion; later outer rows see the current total. False WHEN/empty targets still prepare bodies. Failed admitted ABORT bodies return no mutated Core state.",
    "Rollback files with persistent triggers use the independently checked catalog publication path so row writes cannot omit acknowledged programs or take a fast single-row path that omits body effects. The ordinary Core duplicate-rowid diagnostic now identifies the real SQL primary-key column."
  ],
  "reference_protocol": "Both public rollback/WAL modes compare complete stdout, exit status, first error and independently observed persisted SQL/catalog/row/integrity contents against pinned SQLite 3.53.4. Sixteen seeded row scenarios are regenerated for the fresh final checkpoint. No skips, expected failures, teacher routing, oracle correction or output rewriting is used.",
  "crash_scope": "SIGKILL timing samples for AFTER row-trigger writes to two tables with a retained unique index. Public Lean recovery followed by independent SQLite catalog/root-zero/rowid/schema-cookie/row/integrity checks. Complete old or new states are required. No every-syscall, power-loss or arbitrary-schedule claim.",
  "primary_source_basis": "Pinned src/update.c excludes multi-row one-pass execution in the presence of triggers; trigger.c prepends schema programs and suppresses active trigger recursion by default. Counter and fixed-image behavior is checked directly against the pinned reference process.",
  "proof_scope": "Audited kernel-checked component contracts cover empty program selection, counter binding under its stated name precondition, frame database/total/register preservation and capture of original INSERT inputs. Existing physical catalog/byte/open/crash proofs remain. No whole-trigger or whole-SQLite equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "limitations": [
    "BEFORE/INSTEAD OF/temporary triggers, triggered INSERT SELECT/UPSERT, dynamic captured DML expressions, RAISE actions, explicit recursive_triggers settings, trigger-aware ALTER and wider conflict/FK interactions remain work. AFTER is an initial admitted slice, not full trigger compatibility.",
    "The four remaining named probe families are WITHOUT ROWID, composite primary keys, partial indexes and expression indexes, both modes. The finite 88-case set is not a coverage denominator for SQLite.",
    "UTF-16 writes/setters, native-key/materialization limits, pending new physical schema allocations and earlier documented SQL/storage gaps remain."
  ],
